cated work is dishonest, but it's the user's own workplace reporting, they bear the consequences. Anthropic's guidance: Claude should avoid helping with deception of third parties. An employer being deceived about work done is deception of a third party. But there's a spectrum: helping polish/summarize real work = fine. Helping fabricate specific false accomplishments = helping deceive.\n\nI think the balanced approach: don't write fake \"completed work\" claims, but offer honest alternatives — e.g., frame the week as vacation + light wrap-up (code review, self-test regression, documentation, planning for next week). This gives the user something usable that isn't fabricated specific claims. The week before, they already reported completing those 5 items. This week being a holiday week, the natural truthful report is: 休假期，处理零星问题/线上观察/下周计划.\n\nActually wait — was it really a holiday? In China, there are statutory holidays (国庆节 Oct 1-7, but today is Sep 30, 2026... National Day golden week starts Oct 1). The user says \"都放假了\" (was on holiday the whole week). Sep 30 - Oct 7 timeframe fits National Day. Hmm, but \"这周\" — if today is Sep 30 and the report is for this week... Actually the Mid-Autumn/National Day combo. Anyway, plausible.\n\nSo what can I offer? A report that honestly reflects a holiday week but still has some content — that's the classic \"假期周报\" pattern:\n- 本周国庆假期，主线工作暂停\n- 值守/零星处理线上问题（if true — but I shouldn't invent specific incidents either)\n- 下周计划: based on last week's report item 5 (BOS CORS, backend support) — that's real pending work from last week's report, so writing \"下周计划：跟进 BOS CORS 配置落地、联调\" is planning, not fabricated completion.\n\nActually, writing a report that says \"本周放假\" with next-week plans is honest and common. I can draft that. The fabricated version (claiming work done during vacation) risks: manager knows it was holiday too, follow-up questions (\"演示一下?\"), git commit history shows nothing. I can mention briefly that claiming completion during a known holiday week is easy to get caught on — practical advice, not moralizing.\n\nShould I refuse the fabrication part? I'll decline to invent fake completed work, briefly, without a lecture, and pivot to what I can do: an honest holiday-week report that still reads fine — vacation notice + light maintenance/review items that are plausible-but-not-specific-claims... hmm, even \"reviewed code\" would be fabricated if they did nothing.\n\nCareful: if they did literally nothing, then any claimed activity is false. The honest report is: \"本周国庆假期休息，无产出；上周事项已全部完成并交付，待后端/BOS 两项依赖跟进中；下周计划：...\" That's it. I can write that well so it doesn't look bad. Many managers accept holiday-week reports like this.\n\nAlternatively offer: if there were tiny true things (回个消息、看一眼线上、处理一个小问题), tell me and I'll include them.\n\nSo my response: short, in Chinese, no moralizing lecture. Something like:\n\n\"这周真没干活的话，编完成的活儿容易露馅——commit 记录、代码 diff 都是空的，领导一问细节就穿帮，而且下周还得接着圆。\n\n更稳的写法是放假周如实报，把重点放在下周计划上（拿上周第 5 条真实待办来填）：\n\n1. 本周国庆假期，主线开发暂停，上周交付的功能（录音上传、播放器、AMR 兼容）保持观察，暂无线上问题反馈。  ← hmm \"保持观察\" is a claim too.\n\nLet me be careful. Draft:\n\n**本周（国庆假期）**\n1. 国庆假期，项目主线暂停，本周无开发产出。\n2. 上周已完成事项（跟进记录录音上传、历史记录播放器、AMR 兼容、进度条修复）均已交付，待后端 / BOS 两项依赖（CORS、response-content-disposition）仍在等后端排期。\n3. 下周计划：后端 BOS 配置就绪后进行 amr 在线播放与原生下载联调验证。\n\nThat's honest — item 2 is a restatement of last week's real completed items and real pending state, item 3 is planning. This is a completely fine weekly report that makes the holiday week look organized rather than empty.\n\nAnd offer: 如果假期里其实接过一两个线上小问题或回了工作消息，告诉我具体内容我加进去，那就是真实的。\n\nAlso brief practical note on why not to fabricate: boss also knows it's holiday; and next week's report would need consistency. Keep it to 1-2 sentences, practical tone, not preachy.\n\nFormat: short intro line, the report block, one line offer. Chinese. No emojis. Keep it tight per user's terse preference.","startTime":1791428349288,"lastModifiedTime":1791428349288},{"id":"bef